## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of combining UI state with asynchronous persistence, a common real-world pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Combine debouncing for UI-driven writes
- File I/O and JSON encoding in Swift
- SwiftUI data flow and @Published bindings
- Unit testing asynchronous code and filesystem writes

## Code Example
```swift
import Combine
import SwiftUI

class NotesStore: ObservableObject {
  @Published var note: String = ""
  private var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()
  init() {
    $note
      .debounce(for: .milliseconds(500), scheduler: RunLoop.main)
      .sink { [weak self] text in
        self?.save(text)
      }
      .store(in: &cancellables)
  }
  func save(_ text: String) {
    let json = ["note": text]
    if let data = try? JSONSerialization.data(withJSONObject: json, options: []) {
      let url = FileManager.default.urls(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask)[0]
        .appendingPathComponent("notes.json")
      try? data.write(to: url)
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cancellation of a pending save when the app moves to background?
- How would you extend to multi-note scenarios with conflict resolution?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests CoreData modeling, Combine-based input handling, offline-first UX, and basic testing in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts

- CoreData entity design and relationships (Ride → Driver, Route)
- SwiftUI list driven by NSFetchedResultsController or @FetchRequest
- Combine debounce on text input and error handling
- NSPredicate filtering for search and offline-first consistency
- Basic tests for debounce timing and fetch correctness

## Code Example

```swift
// CoreData models: Ride, Driver, Route
// SwiftUI view: debounced search with 300ms
import SwiftUI
import Combine

class RideViewModel: ObservableObject {
  @Published var searchText: String = ""
  @Published private(set) var results: [Ride] = []
  private var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()
  init(context: NSManagedObjectContext) {
    $searchText
      .debounce(for: .milliseconds(300), scheduler: DispatchQueue.main)
      .sink { text in
        self.fetchRides(matching: text, in: context)
      }
      .store(in: &cancellables)
  }

  private func fetchRides(matching text: String, in context: NSManagedObjectContext) {
    // NSFetchRequest with predicate on destination or route name
    let req: NSFetchRequest<Ride> = Ride.fetchRequest()
    if !text.isEmpty {
      req.predicate = NSPredicate(format: "destination CONTAINS[c] %@", text)
    }
    req.sortDescriptors = [NSSortDescriptor(key: "date", ascending: false)]
    do {
      results = try context.fetch(req)
    } catch {
      print(error)
    }
  }
}

struct RideListView: View {
  @StateObject var vm: RideViewModel
  var body: some View {
    VStack {
      TextField("Search rides…", text: $vm.searchText)
        .padding()
      List(vm.results, id: \.objectID) { ride in
        VStack(alignment: .leading) {
          Text(ride.destination ?? "Unknown")
          Text(ride.date ?? Date(), style: .date)
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

